@startuml pdf-router
' PdfRouter::route — the full backend-selection decision procedure, in evaluation order.
' Render: plantuml -tsvg docs/diagrams/pdf-router.puml
' Source of truth for Figure 2 in docs/components/sources/pdf.md
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
skinparam activity {
  FontColor white
  FontStyle bold
  BorderColor #263238
  BackgroundColor #EF6C00
  DiamondBackgroundColor #FFE0B2
  DiamondFontColor #263238
  DiamondFontStyle plain
  StartColor #00838F
  EndColor #C62828
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #ECEFF1
  BorderColor #546E7A
}

legend top right
|= Concept |= Color |
| routing step | <back:#EF6C00>        </back> |
| predicate | <back:#FFE0B2>        </back> |
endlegend

start
:**PdfRouter::new**
require Marker or Nougat installed
else PdfError::BackendNotAvailable;
:**route(path)**;
if (path.exists()?) then (no)
  :PdfError::FileNotFound;
  stop
endif

:**analyze_document**
fs::metadata ⇒ file_size
quick_pdf_analysis ⇒ (page_count, math_density, has_tables, has_figures)
detect_academic_paper ⇒ filename contains
arxiv|paper|manuscript|preprint|journal|conference|proceedings;

note right
  quick_pdf_analysis reads the **whole**
  file, lossy-decodes it as UTF-8, and
  counts literal substrings:
    page_count  = count('/Type /Page').max(1)
    math_count  = Σ count(26 markers: the word 'equation'
                  plus 25 TeX macros — frac, sum, int, alpha,
                  nabla, mathbb, mathcal, …)
    math_density = min(math_count ÷ (100·page_count), 1)
  Content streams in a real PDF are
  compressed, so these markers rarely
  survive ⇒ math_density ≈ 0 in practice.
end note

if (default_backend ≠ Auto?) then (yes)
  :backend ← default_backend
  reason ← 'Explicitly configured to use …';
  :fallback ← get_fallback(backend)
  if fallback_on_error;
  stop
endif

if (exactly one backend installed?) then (yes)
  :backend ← the installed one
  fallback ← None;
  stop
endif

if (math_density > math_density_threshold?) then (yes)
  :**Nougat**
  high math density;
elseif (page_count > page_count_threshold?) then (yes)
  :**Marker**
  large document — prefer speed;
elseif (is_academic ∧ math_density > 0.1?) then (yes)
  :**Nougat**
  academic paper with math;
else (otherwise)
  :**Marker**
  general-document default;
endif

:fallback ← get_fallback(backend)
if fallback_on_error;
:**RouterDecision**
{ backend, reason, analysis, fallback };
stop
@enduml
